From 1145ba6e103697de7fa57d931f71c27cd42de04d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <81541646+RyanTheTide@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:02:20 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 57/57] tests: Add session lock capture, window list and grab
 tests

Add clients that try to get at what is behind the lock
(session-lock-spy) and cases that check, with the per-frame onscreen
readback of every view still counting leaks:

- screencopy: a screen recorder (copy_with_damage always in flight)
  and screenshot rounds (copy, region, overlay_cursor) while the
  session gets locked, stays locked and is unlocked. Every frame the
  client gets while locked is read back and holds only the blank and
  the lock color; the window animating behind the lock completes no
  damage frame (it does when unlocked).
- screencopy-hotplug: an output plugged in while locked is captured as
  soon as it shows up, black and then the lock color.
- foreign-toplevel: a client bound before the lock gets no event while
  locked (title change, new window, closed window), one bound while
  locked gets no toplevel, minimize/activate/close requests do nothing;
  on unlock both are brought up to date.
- shell-grab: a full screen stage actor added and one raised above the
  lock, a stage grab and key focus on it, the overlay key and Alt+Tab:
  nothing is painted over the lock, the actor gets no event, the keys
  reach the lock client, the focus window does not change.
- window-capture: a window screen cast (capture_into and
  blit_to_framebuffer), paint_to_content and paint_to_bitmap of a
  window give transparent images while locked, a frame is recorded at
  lock and unlock, and none while the window changes behind the lock.

Phases are sync events from the test on the client's own connection, so
an event logged as locked was sent after the compositor held the lock.
Export the screen cast window functions the test calls.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
